$ (containment) takes strings on both sides (diag.dollar_string_only,
warning, on the $ token): a numeric-prefixed operand fires, and
.NOT. "a" $ sList fires because unary .NOT. binds tighter than $, putting
a boolean on the left; the intended test is .NOT. ("a" $ sList).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE HasCode;
	:PARAMETERS nCode, sList;
	:IF nCode $ sList;
		:RETURN .T.;
	:ENDIF;
	:IF .NOT. "a" $ sList;
		:RETURN .F.;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN .NOT. ("b" $ sList);
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE HasCode;
	:PARAMETERS nCode, sList;
	:IF nCode $ sList;
		:RETURN .T.;
	:ENDIF;

	:IF .NOT. "a" $ sList;
		:RETURN .F.;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN .NOT. ("b" $ sList);
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:12-3:13 warning dollar_string_only: The '$' containment operator only works on strings. Non-string operands cause error
6:16-6:17 warning dollar_string_only: The '$' containment operator only works on strings. Non-string operands cause error
